# BLoC Conventions

## Naming

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| BLoC | `<Feature>Bloc` | `AuthBloc` |
| Event | `<Feature><Action>Event` | `AuthLoginEvent` |
| State | `<Feature><Status>State` | `AuthLoginLoadingState` |

## BLoC Responsibilities

BLoC only: dispatch event → call use case → emit state. **No business logic inline.**

```dart
// Correct pattern
await useCase(params).run().then(
  (either) => either.fold(
    (failure) => emit(AuthLoginFailureState(failure)),
    (result) => emit(AuthLoginSuccessState(result)),
  ),
);
```

## Rules

- No `BuildContext` inside BLoC
- No direct `Repository` calls — always via `UseCase`
- No BLoC-to-BLoC direct injection — use shared stream or `EventBus`
- `BlocProvider` in route builder or DI factory — never deep in widget tree
- `HydratedBloc` only for persistence (theme, locale)
- `BaseRequestBloc<T,P>` for standard fetch/refresh/retry — do not re-implement

## Cubit Exception

Cubit allowed only for pure UI state with **no network calls** (e.g. `OtpUiCubit`).
